{"question_text": {"৪৯তম বিসিএস ⎯ ফলিত গণিত (৫৬১)": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) Which of the following is the correct definition of continuity at a point&nbsp;c?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_PfIFynV.png\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_yUp3FVj.png\" width=\"265\" height=\"44\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_1MBDI8I.png\" width=\"269\" height=\"40\">", "option4": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>&nbsp;must be differentiable at&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">c</span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span></span></span></span>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p> Continuity requires that the limit of the function at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">c</span></span> exists and equals the function value at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">c</span></span>. Differentiability is stronger than continuity, so D is wrong.</p>"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Which of the following functions is&nbsp;continuous everywhere&nbsp;on&nbsp;R?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_y8bsrLO.png\" width=\"192\" height=\"64\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_B8s9HE9.png\" width=\"200\" height=\"50\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_eKjo7Gx.png\" width=\"191\" height=\"37\">", "option4": "All of these", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_MsRNWTA.png\" width=\"399\" height=\"90\"></p>"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_UCsCXr1.png\" width=\"531\" height=\"169\">", "option1": "Yes", "option2": "No", "option3": "Only from Left", "option4": "Only from right", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_GWhtnHI.png\" width=\"421\" height=\"86\"></p>"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) If a function is differentiable at&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">x = c</span></span>, then:", "option1": "It must be continuous at&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">c</span></span>.", "option2": "It may or may not be continuous at&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">c.</span></span>", "option3": "It must be discontinuous at&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">c</span></span>.", "option4": "None of the above.", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p>Differentiability implies continuity, but the converse is not always true (e.g. <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(x) = ∣x∣</span></span> continuous at 0 but not differentiable).</p>"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) The function&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(x) = ∣x∣</span></span>&nbsp;at&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">x = 0</span></span> is:", "option1": "Continuous and differentiable", "option2": "Continuous but not differentiable", "option3": "Discontinuous", "option4": "Differentiable but not continuous", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>Continuous at 0, but left derivative = - 1, right derivative = 1. So, not differentiable.</p>"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) Which of the following functions satisfies Rolle’s theorem on [0, π]?", "option1": "<span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(x) = sin⁡x</span>", "option2": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">) </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mop\">cos</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x&nbsp;</span></span>", "option3": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">) </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x<sup>2</sup></span></span></span>", "option4": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">) </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><sup><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">x</span></span></span></span></span></span></sup></span></span>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<ul data-start=\"645\" data-end=\"847\">\r\n<li data-start=\"645\" data-end=\"715\">\r\n<p data-start=\"647\" data-end=\"715\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">f(x) = sinx </span>: f(0) = 0,f(π) = 0.  Conditions satisfied.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"716\" data-end=\"761\">\r\n<p data-start=\"718\" data-end=\"761\">f(x) = cos⁡x : endpoints different.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"762\" data-end=\"804\">\r\n<p data-start=\"764\" data-end=\"804\">f(x) = x<sup>2</sup> : endpoints not equal. </p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"805\" data-end=\"847\">\r\n<p data-start=\"807\" data-end=\"847\">f(x) = ex : endpoints not equal</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) If&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(x) = x<sup>2</sup></span></span>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">[1, 3</span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mclose\">]</span></span></span></span>, then by Mean Value Theorem, there exists&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">c ∈ (1, 3</span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> such that:", "option1": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f’</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mclose\">) </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span>", "option2": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f’</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mclose\">) </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">3</span></span>", "option3": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">’</span></span></span>(c) = 4</span></span>", "option4": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f’</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mclose\">) </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">5</span></span>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_Aqbpcwa.png\" width=\"299\" height=\"57\"></p>"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_EYJQapJ.png\" width=\"736\" height=\"68\">", "option1": "0", "option2": "1", "option3": "2", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "2", "exp": "<ul data-start=\"3168\" data-end=\"3428\">\r\n<li data-start=\"3168\" data-end=\"3304\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3170\" data-end=\"3195\">First check conditions:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3198\" data-end=\"3304\">\r\n<li data-start=\"3198\" data-end=\"3231\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3200\" data-end=\"3231\">Continuous? Yes (polynomial).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3234\" data-end=\"3258\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3236\" data-end=\"3258\">Differentiable? Yes.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3261\" data-end=\"3304\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3263\" data-end=\"3304\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> → equal endpoints.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3305\" data-end=\"3349\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3307\" data-end=\"3349\">Apply Rolle’s theorem: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f′(x)=2x−2</span></span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3350\" data-end=\"3403\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3352\" data-end=\"3403\">Solve <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mrel\">⟹</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mrel\">⟹</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) Cauchy’s Mean Value Theorem generalizes the MVT by involving two functions&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f,g</span></span>. Its result is:", "option1": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f‘</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mclose\">) </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span>", "option2": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">g‘</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c</span><span class=\"mclose\">) </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span>", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_etp7h2O.png\" width=\"234\" height=\"64\">", "option4": "Both A and B", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_ohc14ON.png\" width=\"704\" height=\"154\"></p>"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) If&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(x) = </span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span></span></span></span>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">[- 1, 1</span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mclose\">]</span></span></span></span>, does Rolle’s theorem apply?", "option1": "Yes, because&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(-1) = f(1)</span></span>", "option2": "No, because&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(x)</span></span>&nbsp;is not continuous on&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">[- 1, 1]</span></span>", "option3": "No, because&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(x)</span></span>&nbsp;is not differentiable at&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">x = 0</span></span>", "option4": "Yes, because derivative exists at all&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">x ≠ 0</span></span>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p>Function: f(x)=∣x∣ on [−1,1].</p>\r\n<p>Conditions for Rolle’s theorem:</p>\r\n<p>f continuous on [a,b] → true.<br>f differentiable on (a,b) → fails at x=0.<br>f(a)=f(b)⟹f(−1)=f(1)=1 →  true.<br>Since differentiability fails at 0, Rolle’s theorem does not apply.</p>\r\n<p>Correct: C</p>"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_fgI4AlJ.png\" width=\"952\" height=\"70\">", "option1": "1", "option2": "2", "option3": "3", "option4": "4", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_8CJAYW2.png\" width=\"405\" height=\"129\"></p>"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) For&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(x) = sin⁡(2x)</span></span>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">[0, π]</span></span>, find all possible&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">c</span></span> given by Rolle’s theorem.", "option1": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">c = π/4</span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> only", "option2": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">c = π/4, 3π/4</span></span>", "option3": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">c </span><span class=\"mrel\">= 0</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mpunct\">, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">π</span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span></span>", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_zJKmwlD.png\" width=\"576\" height=\"148\"></p>"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_QxOOOwJ.png\" width=\"952\" height=\"64\">", "option1": "<span class=\"katex-mathml\">e<sup>c </sup>= 1</span>", "option2": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><sup><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">c</span></span></span></span></span></span> </sup></span><span class=\"mrel\">= e</span></span>", "option3": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><sup><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">c</span></span></span></span></span></span> </sup></span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e - </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span>", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_ypJ7lc3.png\" width=\"397\" height=\"199\"></p>"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_WvCCP7K.png\" width=\"883\" height=\"51\">", "option1": "0", "option2": "π/4", "option3": "<span class=\"mord\">π/2</span>", "option4": "π", "answer": "3", "exp": "<ul data-start=\"143\" data-end=\"419\">\r\n<li data-start=\"143\" data-end=\"290\">\r\n<p data-start=\"145\" data-end=\"181\"><strong data-start=\"145\" data-end=\"156\">Step 1:</strong> Check Rolle’s theorem:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"184\" data-end=\"290\">\r\n<li data-start=\"184\" data-end=\"211\">\r\n<p data-start=\"186\" data-end=\"211\">Continuous on [0, π]? </p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"214\" data-end=\"245\">\r\n<p data-start=\"216\" data-end=\"245\">Differentiable on (0, π)? </p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"248\" data-end=\"290\">\r\n<p data-start=\"250\" data-end=\"290\">Endpoints equal? <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(0)=f(π)=0</span></span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"292\" data-end=\"345\">\r\n<p data-start=\"294\" data-end=\"345\"><strong data-start=\"294\" data-end=\"305\">Step 2:</strong> Find derivative: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mop\">cos</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"347\" data-end=\"419\">\r\n<p data-start=\"349\" data-end=\"419\"><strong data-start=\"349\" data-end=\"360\">Step 3:</strong> Solve <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f′(c)=0</span></span>: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">cos⁡c=0  ⟹  c=π/2</span></span></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_x8oKek0.png\" width=\"1018\" height=\"56\">", "option1": "c = - 1, 0, 1", "option2": "c = 1 only", "option3": "c = - 1 only", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_5GCq4SA.png\" width=\"435\" height=\"31\"><br><br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_g0gbhWX.png\" width=\"172\" height=\"17\"><br><br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_HAVypAP.png\" width=\"301\" height=\"54\"><br><br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_YWxAyN7.png\" width=\"359\" height=\"86\"></p>"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) Which of the following is&nbsp;necessary for Rolle’s theorem to hold?", "option1": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mclose\">) </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span>", "option2": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>&nbsp;continuous on&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">[a, b]</span></span>", "option3": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(x)</span></span>&nbsp;differentiable on&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">(a, b)</span></span>", "option4": "All of the above", "answer": "4", "exp": ""}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_v3VNd8n.png\" width=\"805\" height=\"40\">", "option1": "c = 3/2", "option2": "c = 2/√3", "option3": "c = 0", "option4": "c = 1", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_p6O2zac.png\" width=\"311\" height=\"56\"><br><br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_R3YYgrp.png\" width=\"181\" height=\"28\"></p>"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) Which of the following is&nbsp;true?", "option1": "Rolle’s theorem is a special case of MVT", "option2": "MVT is a special case of Rolle’s theorem", "option3": "Rolle’s theorem and MVT are not related", "option4": "&nbsp;None of the above", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p data-start=\"3081\" data-end=\"3158\">Rolle’s Theorem is the case of MVT when <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(a) = f(b)</span></span>.</p>"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_I0ksWqe.png\" width=\"825\" height=\"37\">", "option1": "0", "option2": "1", "option3": "2", "option4": "3", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_bGghpKq.png\" width=\"616\" height=\"59\"></p>"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_OE5uEgI.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"703\" height=\"61\">", "option1": "0", "option2": "1", "option3": "2", "option4": "Does not exist", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_RlO3fCE.png\" width=\"581\" height=\"51\"></p>"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) A function&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(x, y)</span></span>&nbsp;is continuous at&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">(a, b</span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> if:", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_hgbIY75.png\" width=\"287\" height=\"43\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_2IfHgKW.png\" width=\"207\" height=\"46\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_FnAyKW6.png\" width=\"309\" height=\"33\">", "option4": "All of these", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p data-start=\"1224\" data-end=\"1325\">Generalization of single - variable continuity to several variables.</p>"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_4NGGL2c.png\" width=\"553\" height=\"106\">", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_CtwLgmx.png\" width=\"131\" height=\"77\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_QzRxAEO.png\" width=\"114\" height=\"71\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_etJ6s8x.png\" width=\"211\" height=\"46\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_TXvC8FW.png\" width=\"143\" height=\"86\">", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip5_x4vRsVi.png\" width=\"491\" height=\"40\"></p>"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_KP2vpYw.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"519\" height=\"123\">", "option1": "1", "option2": "x", "option3": "y", "option4": "z", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_vG9o8UU.png\" width=\"331\" height=\"41\"></p>"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) Schwarz’s theorem states that if&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(x, y)</span></span>&nbsp;has continuous second partial derivatives:", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip6_CdFyiQv.png\" width=\"189\" height=\"75\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_SpaYy3j.png\" width=\"168\" height=\"79\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip5_QeCSqRJ.png\" width=\"183\" height=\"94\">", "option4": "None of the above", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip7_9UHfeH1.png\" width=\"518\" height=\"96\"></p>"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) Which one is true?", "option1": "Young’s theorem is a&nbsp;generalization of Schwarz’s theorem", "option2": "&nbsp;Schwarz’s theoremis a generalization of Young’s theorem.", "option3": "Young’s theorem is a&nbsp;generalization of Mean Value Theorem.", "option4": "Schwarz’s theoremis a generalization of Taylor's Theorem.", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p>Young’s theorem provides conditions for equality of mixed partials even when continuity is weaker than Schwarz’s theorem.</p>"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_5pqdjAi.png\" width=\"383\" height=\"135\">", "option1": "0", "option2": "1", "option3": "Does not exist", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_NA4Z24x.png\" width=\"645\" height=\"93\"></p>"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_hF0YJIA.png\" width=\"487\" height=\"99\">", "option1": "&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">6xy + 5</span></span>", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_Ej5HLie.png\" width=\"137\" height=\"48\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_mRWy2pH.png\" width=\"132\" height=\"49\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_86Muz3m.png\" width=\"133\" height=\"51\">", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_8jbOHM1.png\"></p>"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) Young’s theorem is applicable when", "option1": "The function is differentiable but not continuous", "option2": "The mixed partial derivatives exist and are continuous", "option3": "The function is linear", "option4": "The limit exists along all paths but is path-dependent", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>Young's theorem is essentially the same as Schwarz’s or Clairaut’s theorem for functions of two variables, stating that if f_xy and f_yx exist and are continuous in an open region, then they are equal at every point in that region. The key is the continuity of the second partials, which guarantees commutativity of differentiation.</p>"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) Which of the following is&nbsp;continuous everywhere?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_kBvoZpm.png\" width=\"144\" height=\"49\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_tTAwtYF.png\" width=\"172\" height=\"42\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_De00xOA.png\" width=\"157\" height=\"47\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_5PDcmEa.png\" width=\"203\" height=\"52\">", "answer": "3", "exp": "<ul data-start=\"465\" data-end=\"635\">\r\n<li data-start=\"465\" data-end=\"503\">\r\n<p data-start=\"467\" data-end=\"503\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">sin⁡x/x</span></span> not defined at 0.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"504\" data-end=\"545\">\r\n<p data-start=\"506\" data-end=\"545\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">ln⁡x</span></span> undefined at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"546\" data-end=\"583\">\r\n<p data-start=\"548\" data-end=\"583\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">e<sup>x</sup></span></span> continuous everywhere</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"584\" data-end=\"635\">\r\n<p data-start=\"586\" data-end=\"635\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">tan⁡x</span></span> has poles at odd multiples of π/2</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) Which function is differentiable everywhere?", "option1": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">।x।</span></span>", "option2": "<span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x<sup>2</sup></span></span><span class=\"mop\">sin</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span>", "option3": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">x/।x।</span></span>", "option4": "All Of these", "answer": "2", "exp": "<ul data-start=\"821\" data-end=\"1074\">\r\n<li data-start=\"821\" data-end=\"859\">\r\n<p data-start=\"823\" data-end=\"859\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">∣</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mord\">∣</span></span></span></span> not differentiable at 0.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"860\" data-end=\"917\">\r\n<p data-start=\"862\" data-end=\"917\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">x<sup>2</sup>sin⁡x</span></span> smooth → differentiable everywhere</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1043\" data-end=\"1074\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1045\" data-end=\"1074\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">x/∣x∣</span></span> undefined at 0.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>"}, {"id": "31", "question": "৩১) For&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(x) = √x</span></span> on [0, 1], why does Rolle’s theorem fail?", "option1": "Not continuous", "option2": "Not differentiable at 0", "option3": "Endpoints not equal", "option4": "None", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_2PisYon.png\" width=\"202\" height=\"49\"><br><br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_BOHU1Kz.png\" width=\"254\" height=\"57\"><br><br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_efxRDwb.png\" width=\"269\" height=\"27\"></p>"}, {"id": "32", "question": "৩২) For&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">) </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><sup><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span></span></span> </sup></span><span class=\"mbin\">- </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> on [- 1, 1], c is:", "option1": "0", "option2": "- 1", "option3": "1", "option4": "None of these", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_ZCFSY2l.png\" width=\"323\" height=\"131\"></p>"}, {"id": "33", "question": "৩৩) Mean Value Theorem guarantees:", "option1": "A point where tangent is parallel to secant", "option2": "Function must be constant", "option3": "Function must be increasing", "option4": "Tangent = normal", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p>That’s the geometric meaning of MVT.<br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_enluOO3.png\" width=\"483\" height=\"165\"></p>"}, {"id": "34", "question": "৩৪) Let&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(x)=x</span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord sqrt\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span>&nbsp;on&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">[0,4]</span></span>. Which is true?", "option1": "Rolle’s theorem applies", "option2": "Mean Value Theorem applies", "option3": "Neither applies.", "option4": "Both apply.", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span></span></span></span> is continuous on [0,4], differentiable on (0,4), so MVT applies. Rolle does not because <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(0)≠f(4)</span></span>.</p>"}, {"id": "35", "question": "৩৫) The Cauchy Mean Value Theorem reduces to the ordinary Mean Value Theorem when:", "option1": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">) </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">g</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span>", "option2": "<span class=\"base\">